From 6107fcd759e265d8d2b4393073e07865fb92bf18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mixadod <mixadod123@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:27:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Wayland -> X11 drag and drop

Nothing dragged from a Wayland client (a file manager) could be dropped on
an X11 window: satellite had no drag-and-drop bridge. Satellite now plays
the XDND source for a Wayland drag over one of its X windows:

- finds the XdndAware window under the pointer, honouring XdndProxy;
- sends XdndEnter (XdndTypeList past three types), XdndPosition,
  XdndLeave and XdndDrop;
- maps XdndStatus to wl_data_offer.accept/set_actions, XdndFinished to
  wl_data_offer.finish;
- answers XdndSelection conversions from the Wayland offer.

The action is always copy, so the Wayland source never deletes a file
after a "move" it thinks happened.

Reading from a Wayland source (drops and the clipboard) now gives up after
2 s without data instead of blocking forever, which froze every X client
when a source hung.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
